jolt-autobahn/launch.sh\\\\\\\" *command-line-args*)}\\\\n\\\\n  deps:npm\\\\n  {:doc \\\\\\\"Worktree-local npm ci, reused only while input and installed-file digests match\\\\\\\"\\\\n   :task (shell \\\\\\\"bb\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"src/dev/build_cache.clj\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"npm\\\\\\\")}\\\\n\\\\n  ;; jolt host lane (experimental, docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md)\\\\n  bootstrap:jolt\\\\n  {:doc \\\\\\\"Materialize the jolt-toolchain.edn pins into build/tools/jolt (mise Chez/CMake checked, jolt cloned at the full SHA, never pulled) and write build/tools/jolt-env.sh\\\\\\\"\\\\n   :task (System/exit\\\\n           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \\\\\\\"bb\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj\\\\\\\")))}\\\\n\\\\n  test:jolt-bootstrap-neg\\\\n  {:doc \\\\\\\"Copy/revert the jolt clone under gitignored build/bootstrap-neg (deleted on success, retained on failure) and declare a synthetic patch and prove bootstrap refuses it unapplied or corrupted, then accepts it applied (JOLT_BOOTSTRAP_TEST_DIR selects the source clone)\\\\\\\"\\\\n   :task (System/exit\\\\n           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \\\\\\\"bb\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"src/dev/jolt_bootstrap.clj\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"--test-negative\\\\\\\")))}\\\\n\\\\n  smoke:jolt\\\\n  {:doc \\\\\\\"J0a baseline smoke under jolt -Srepro -M:jolt: tracked load of yang.antlr.export/packet and defcfn :blocking calls (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\\\\\\\"\\\\n   :task (System/exit\\\\n           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \\\\\\\"sh\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"-c\\\\\\\"\\\\n                         \\\\\\\". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_smoke.clj\\\\\\\")))}\\\\n\\\\n  jolt\\\\n  {:doc \\\\\\\"Run jolt -Srepro -M:jolt with the arguments given (a script path, -e ...), under build/tools/jolt-env.sh\\\\\\\"\\\\n   :task (System/exit\\\\n           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \\\\\\\"sh\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"-c\\\\\\\"\\\\n                         \\\\\\\". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && exec \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$@\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n                         \\\\\\\"jolt\\\\\\\" *command-line-args*)))}\\\\n\\\\n  qualify:jolt-libcrypto\\\\n  {:doc \\\\\\\"J1b requalification: print this platform's observed libcrypto identity {:canonical-path :version-num :version :sha256} for jolt-toolchain.edn :native :libcrypto :qualified (the digest from bb and from the library, required equal); changes nothing (needs a built wrapper: bb build:jolt-native, or --requalify after a library change)\\\\\\\"\\\\n   :task (System/exit\\\\n           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \\\\\\\"bb\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"native/jolt-crypto/qualify.clj\\\\\\\")))}\\\\n\\\\n  probe:jolt-crypto\\\\n  {:doc \\\\\\\"J1b: libcrypto provenance (qualified, missing, undeclared, version-floor, wrong-library-first, Linux LD_PRELOAD) and 256 MiB :blocking hash collect-safety, each in a child jolt process (needs bb build:jolt-native)\\\\\\\"\\\\n   :task (System/exit\\\\n           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \\\\\\\"bb\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"native/jolt-crypto/probes/run.clj\\\\\\\")))}\\\\n\\\\n  test:jolt-j5\\\\n  {:doc \\\\\\\"J5 acceptance: one Python session through the JVM and jolt REPL entry points with the standard catalog (output equal line for line), the multiline probe sequence, and the unavailable-library REPL legs (needs bb build:jolt-native)\\\\\\\"\\\\n   :task (System/exit\\\\n           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \\\\\\\"bb\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"src/dev/jolt_j5_acceptance.clj\\\\\\\")))}\\\\n\\\\n  probe:jolt-j5\\\\n  {:doc \\\\\\\"J5b: the native Python parser's budget (input 4 MiB; in-parser guards: 8192 rule frames, 4096 SLL lookahead links, 256 full-LL links, on a 16 MiB parse thread): the review's repros, at/over per shape against the predicted table, 10x the old crash depths, the JVM's packets (incl. a 20,000-deep 1+ tree), the old crash depths in children on the jolt thread, injected C++ faults, the abort-is-a-failure property, lifecycle and unavailable-library legs. Args select legs: budget below crash inject abort unavailable (needs bb build:jolt-native)\\\\\\\"\\\\n   :task (System/exit\\\\n           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \\\\\\\"bb\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"src/dev/jolt_j5_run.clj\\\\\\\" *command-line-args*)))}\\\\n\\\\n  calibrate:jolt-j5\\\\n  {:doc \\\\\\\"J5b C4 + J5c: build the guards-off calibration variant of native/jolt-parser and record each nesting shape's stack cost per rule frame and per lookahead link on the 16 MiB parse thread (asserting every bound fits a quarter of the stack; writes build/j5b/calibration.edn), or, with --work, the work metric's per-shape counts and the corpus sweep the work bound derives from (writes build/j5b/work.edn; needs bb build:jolt-native)\\\\\\\"\\\\n   :task (System/exit\\\\n           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \\\\\\\"bb\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"-cp\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"src/dev\\\\\\\"\\\\n                         \\\\\\\"src/dev/jolt_j5_calibrate.clj\\\\\\\" *command-line-args*)))}\\\\n\\\\n  probe:jolt-file\\\\n  {:doc \\\\\\\"J4a: native/jolt-file gates, each in a child process: JVM-identical frame bytes (both hash algorithms), F2 s32BE prefixes, strict reads, injected short/EINTR/zero-progress/error transfers, corrupt-open byte identity, idempotent close, no fd or native-memory leak, a full collection during a 1 GiB :blocking pwrite, missing/wrong-layout wrapper refused before guest work, exported-symbol allowlist (needs bb build:jolt-native)\\\\\\\"\\\\n   :task (System/exit\\\\n           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \\\\\\\"bb\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"native/jolt-file/probes/run.clj\\\\\\\")))}\\\\n\\\\n  probe:jolt-udp\\\\n  {:doc \\\\\\\"J0b probe: raw nonblocking SOCK_DGRAM over jolt.ffi on macOS arm64 and Linux x86_64, printing the platform header first (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\\\\\\\"\\\\n   :task (System/exit\\\\n           (:exit (shell {:continue true} \\\\\\\"sh\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.sh\\\\\\\")))}\\\\n\\\\n  probe:jolt-tcp\\\\n  {:doc \\\\\\\"J6d: the jolt TCP substrate and owner-thread pump (dao.stream.ws.tcp, dao.stream.ws.pump, driver sleep-fds!), one child jolt process per section: closure (no jolt.socket), address (literals/localhost, resolver trap), substrate (port 0, nonblocking accept/connect, EOF vs reset, gone-peer write survives), ordered (A3 short write, drain order, failure), fairness (A1 ii/iv), stdin (A1 i, held partial line), deadline (A2 seam), control (A3 event orders, A4 pong budget, D1 close slot), close (A5, D2, D3), listener (64 cap, lower-deadlines!, drained?); native memory and registry empty after close. Arguments select sections (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\\\\\\\"\\\\n   :task (let [sections (or (seq *command-line-args*)\\\\n                            [\\\\\\\"closure\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"address\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"substrate\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"ordered\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"fairness\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"stdin\\\\\\\"\\\\n                             \\\\\\\"deadline\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"control\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"close\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"listener\\\\\\\"])\\\\n               results (mapv (fn [s]\\\\n                               (println \\\\\\\"== probe:jolt-tcp section\\\\\\\" s)\\\\n                               [s (:exit (shell {:continue true} \\\\\\\"sh\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"-c\\\\\\\"\\\\n                                                \\\\\\\". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && exec \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_tcp_probe.clj \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n                                                \\\\\\\"jolt\\\\\\\" s))])\\\\n                             sections)]\\\\n           (println \\\\\\\"probe:jolt-tcp exits\\\\\\\" (pr-str results))\\\\n           (System/exit (if (every? (comp zero? second) results) 0 1)))}\\\\n\\\\n  probe:jolt-ws\\\\n  {:doc \\\\\\\"J6e: the jolt WebSocket host adapter (dao.stream.ws.jolt, the yin.repl.host shadow, the jolt -main wiring), one child jolt process per section: closure (C1), handshake (C2), bind (C3), address (C4), io (C5), close (C6), shutdown (C7, the real owner loop), isolation (C8), driver (C9, deadline folding, a --headless --port child), fairness (C10); native memory and registries empty after close. Arguments select sections (needs bb bootstrap:jolt and bb build:jolt-native)\\\\\\\"\\\\n   :task (let [sections (or (seq *command-line-args*)\\\\n                            [\\\\\\\"closure\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"handshake\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"bind\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"address\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"io\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"close\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"shutdown\\\\\\\"\\\\n                             \\\\\\\"isolation\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"driver\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"fairness\\\\\\\"])\\\\n               results (mapv (fn [s]\\\\n                               (println \\\\\\\"== probe:jolt-ws section\\\\\\\" s)\\\\n                               [s (:exit (shell {:continue true} \\\\\\\"sh\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"-c\\\\\\\"\\\\n                                                \\\\\\\". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && exec \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_ws_probe.clj \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n                                                \\\\\\\"jolt\\\\\\\" s))])\\\\n                             sections)]\\\\n           (println \\\\\\\"probe:jolt-ws exits\\\\\\\" (pr-str results))\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ncollab/yang-php/1794566777000-engineer-p7b-ticks-b.gpt-6.1-terra.stdout.log:22:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_10\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '370,550p' src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj; cat test/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj | head -55; cat docs/agents/build-n-test.md | head -100\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"   (a path relative to `<dir>`) as `auto_prepend_file`, and return the\\\\n   parsed `{:out :diag :uncaught :exit}`.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [dir file prepend-file]\\\\n  (let [{:keys [out err exit]}\\\\n        (sh/sh \\\\\\\"docker\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"run\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"--rm\\\\\\\"\\\\n               \\\\\\\"-v\\\\\\\" (str (.toAbsolutePath (.toPath (io/file dir))) \\\\\\\":/w\\\\\\\")\\\\n               \\\\\\\"-w\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"/w\\\\\\\"\\\\n               \\\\\\\"php:8.3-cli\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"php\\\\\\\"\\\\n               \\\\\\\"-d\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"display_errors=1\\\\\\\"\\\\n               \\\\\\\"-d\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"html_errors=0\\\\\\\"\\\\n               \\\\\\\"-d\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"error_reporting=E_ALL\\\\\\\"\\\\n               \\\\\\\"-d\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"log_errors=0\\\\\\\"\\\\n               \\\\\\\"-d\\\\\\\" (str \\\\\\\"auto_prepend_file=/w/\\\\\\\" prepend-file)\\\\n               file\\\\n               :out-enc \\\\\\\"UTF-8\\\\\\\")]\\\\n    (assoc (parse-stdout out file nil)\\\\n           :err err\\\\n           :exit exit)))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn check-p5-fixture\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Run P5 `fixture` in temporary directory `dir`: the fixture source plus,\\\\n   for `:request`-bearing fixtures, the [[p5-prologue]] as\\\\n   `auto_prepend_file`. Returns a check record like [[check-fixture]].\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [dir {:keys [id source request out diag uncaught status oracle]}]\\\\n  (let [file (str (name id) \\\\\\\".php\\\\\\\")\\\\n        pre (str (name id) \\\\\\\"-pre.php\\\\\\\")]\\\\n    (write-source! dir file source)\\\\n    (when request (write-source! dir pre (p5-prologue request)))\\\\n    (let [actual (if request\\\\n                   (run-php-file-with-prepend dir file pre)\\\\n                   (run-php-file dir file))\\\\n          expected-out (or out \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\")\\\\n          expected-diag (vec (or diag []))\\\\n          pass? (and (not= :pending oracle)\\\\n                     (= expected-out (:out actual))\\\\n                     (diag-match? expected-diag (:diag actual))\\\\n                     (= uncaught (:uncaught actual))\\\\n                     (or (nil? status) (= status (:exit actual))))]\\\\n      {:id id,\\\\n       :pass? pass?,\\\\n       :oracle oracle,\\\\n       :expected {:out expected-out, :diag expected-diag, :uncaught uncaught, :status status},\\\\n       :actual (assoc (select-keys actual [:out :diag :uncaught]) :exit (:exit actual))})))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn run-p5\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Run all `p5/fixtures` (the request-context fixtures) against\\\\n   `php:8.3-cli`.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  []\\\\n  (let [dir (.toFile (Files/createTempDirectory \\\\\\\"yang-php-oracle-p5-\\\\\\\"\\\\n                                                (make-array FileAttribute 0)))]\\\\n    (try\\\\n      (mapv #(check-p5-fixture dir %) p5/fixtures)\\\\n      (finally\\\\n        (doseq [f (reverse (file-seq dir))]\\\\n          (.delete ^java.io.File f))))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn check-p5b2-fixture\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Run P5b2 `fixture` in temporary directory `dir`: the fixture source plus\\\\n   the [[p5b2-prologue]] as `auto_prepend_file` (the ruled recursive merge\\\\n   and, for `:http-profile` fixtures, the explicit initial status 200 — bare\\\\n   CLI starts without the engine's assumed HTTP 200). Returns a check record\\\\n   like [[check-fixture]], with the engine's guest-fatal representation\\\\n   (`:fatal`) compared against the parser's preserved `:fatal`.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [dir {:keys [id source out diag uncaught status fatal oracle]}]\\\\n  (let [file (str (name id) \\\\\\\".php\\\\\\\")\\\\n        pre (str (name id) \\\\\\\"-pre.php\\\\\\\")\\\\n        fixture (first (filter #(= id (:id %)) p5b2/fixtures))]\\\\n    (write-source! dir file source)\\\\n    (write-source! dir pre (p5b2-prologue fixture))\\\\n    (let [actual (run-php-file-with-prepend dir file pre)\\\\n          expected-out (or out \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\")\\\\n          expected-diag (vec (or diag []))\\\\n          pass? (and (not= :pending oracle)\\\\n                     (= expected-out (:out actual))\\\\n                     (diag-match? expected-diag (:diag actual))\\\\n                     (= uncaught (:uncaught actual))\\\\n                     (= fatal (:fatal actual))\\\\n                     (or (nil? status) (= status (:exit actual))))]\\\\n      {:id id,\\\\n       :pass? pass?,\\\\n       :oracle oracle,\\\\n       :expected {:out expected-out, :diag expected-diag, :uncaught uncaught,\\\\n                  :fatal fatal, :status status},\\\\n       :actual (assoc (select-keys actual [:out :diag :uncaught :fatal]) :exit (:exit actual))})))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn run-p5b2\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Run all `p5b2/fixtures` (the B2 step-7 fixtures) against `php:8.3-cli`.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  []\\\\n  (let [dir (.toFile (Files/createTempDirectory \\\\\\\"yang-php-oracle-p5b2-\\\\\\\"\\\\n                                                (make-array FileAttribute 0)))]\\\\n    (try\\\\n      (mapv #(check-p5b2-fixture dir %) p5b2/fixtures)\\\\n      (finally\\\\n        (doseq [f (reverse (file-seq dir))]\\\\n          (.delete ^java.io.File f))))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn print-fold\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Print the fold lines for `results`: one paste-ready record per fixture\\\\n   in the P4 [[p4/pin]] shape `{:oracle p5-banner :out :diag :uncaught}`,\\\\n   carrying the guest-fatal representation (`:fatal`) and the process exit\\\\n   status (`:status`) alongside.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [results]\\\\n  (doseq [{:keys [id actual]} results]\\\\n    (println \\\\\\\"FOLD\\\\\\\" (name id)\\\\n             (pr-str (assoc (select-keys actual [:out :diag :uncaught :fatal])\\\\n                            :oracle p5-banner\\\\n                            :status (:exit actual))))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn run-all\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Run all `programs/fixtures`, `matrix-source` and `float-cases` against\\\\n   `php:8.3-cli`.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  []\\\\n  (let [dir (.toFile (Files/createTempDirectory \\\\\\\"yang-php-oracle-\\\\\\\"\\\\n                                                (make-array FileAttribute 0)))]\\\\n    (try\\\\n      (-> (mapv #(check-fixture dir %) (concat programs/fixtures p3b/all-fixtures p4/all-fixtures p6/all-fixtures))\\\\n          (conj (check-matrix dir))\\\\n          (conj (check-floats dir)))\\\\n      (finally\\\\n        (doseq [f (reverse (file-seq dir))]\\\\n          (.delete ^java.io.File f))))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn -main\\\\n  [& args]\\\\n  (when (some #{\\\\\\\"--print-prologue\\\\\\\"} args)\\\\n    (let [id (keyword (or (second (drop-while #(not= \\\\\\\"--print-prologue\\\\\\\" %) args))\\\\n                          \\\\\\\"superglobals-from-request\\\\\\\"))\\\\n          fixture (first (filter #(= id (:id %)) p5/fixtures))\\\\n          b2-fixture (first (filter #(= id (:id %)) p5b2/fixtures))]\\\\n      (when-not (or fixture b2-fixture)\\\\n        (println \\\\\\\"Unknown P5 fixture:\\\\\\\" id)\\\\n        (System/exit 2))\\\\n      ;; Dry run: no docker, no oracle. Print the generated prologue for\\\\n      ;; eyeball comparison against the engine's expected superglobal\\\\n      ;; values (the fixture's hand-derived :out is the reference).\\\\n      (print (if b2-fixture\\\\n               (p5b2-prologue b2-fixture)\\\\n               (p5-prologue (:request fixture))))\\\\n      (flush)\\\\n      (shutdown-agents)\\\\n      (System/exit 0)))\\\\n  (when (some #{\\\\\\\"--p5\\\\\\\"} args)\\\\n    (let [results (run-p5)\\\\n          recorded (filter #(= :pending (:oracle %)) results)\\\\n          failures (remove #(or (:pass? %) (= :pending (:oracle %))) results)]\\\\n      (println \\\\\\\"Banner:\\\\\\\" p5-banner)\\\\n      (println \\\\\\\"Checked:\\\\\\\" (count results) \\\\\\\"P5 targets; failures:\\\\\\\" (count failures))\\\\n      (print-fold recorded)\\\\n      (doseq [f failures]\\\\n        (println \\\\\\\"FAIL\\\\\\\" (:id f))\\\\n        (println \\\\\\\"  expected:\\\\\\\" (pr-str (:expected f)))\\\\n        (println \\\\\\\"  actual:  \\\\\\\" (pr-str (:actual f))))\\\\n      (shutdown-agents)\\\\n      (when (seq failures)\\\\n        (System/exit 1))\\\\n      (System/exit 0)))\\\\n  (when (some #{\\\\\\\"--p5b2\\\\\\\"} args)\\\\n    (let [results (run-p5b2)\\\\n          recorded (filter #(= :pending (:oracle %)) results)\\\\n          failures (remove #(or (:pass? %) (= :pending (:oracle %))) results)]\\\\n      (println \\\\\\\"Banner:\\\\\\\" p5-banner)\\\\n      (println \\\\\\\"Checked:\\\\\\\" (count results) \\\\\\\"P5b2 targets; failures:\\\\\\\" (count failures))\\\\n      (print-fold recorded)\\\\n      (doseq [f failures]\\\\n        (println \\\\\\\"FAIL\\\\\\\" (:id f))\\\\n        (println \\\\\\\"  expected:\\\\\\\" (pr-str (:expected f)))\\\\n        (println \\\\\\\"  actual:  \\\\\\\" (pr-str (:actual f))))\\\\n      (shutdown-agents)\\\\n      (when (seq failures)\\\\n        (System/exit 1))\\\\n      (System/exit 0)))\\\\n  (let [results (run-all)\\\\n        recorded (filter #(= :pending (:oracle %)) results)\\\\n        failures (remove #(or (:pass? %) (= :pending (:oracle %))) results)]\\\\n(ns yang.php.antlr.generators-test\\\\n  \\\\\\\"P4 S8 generators, live iteration and protocol integration on the JVM.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  (:require\\\\n    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\\\n    [yang.php.antlr.e2e-harness :as h]\\\\n    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p4 :as p4]\\\\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\\\\n    [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\\\\n    [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\\\\n    [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\\\\n    [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\\\\n    [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\\\\n    [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as sr-linearize]\\\\n    [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\\\\n    [yin.vm.values :as values])\\\\n  (:import\\\\n    [java.util IdentityHashMap]))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(def ^:private vms [:ast-walker :semantic :stack :register])\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(deftest generator-fixtures-on-every-vm-test\\\\n  (doseq [{:keys [id source out]} p4/generators-v1]\\\\n    (testing (name id)\\\\n      (let [results (h/run-php source)]\\\\n        (is (not (contains? results :diagnostics)) (pr-str results))\\\\n        (doseq [k vms]\\\\n          (is (= out (get results k)) (str (name id) \\\\\\\" on \\\\\\\" k)))))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(deftest iteration-protocols-test\\\\n  (testing \\\\\\\"Iterator drives foreach directly\\\\\\\"\\\\n    (is (= \\\\\\\"01\\\\\\\" (:php/out (h/run-raw\\\\n                            \\\\\\\"<?php class I implements Iterator { private $i=0; function rewind(): void {$this->i=0;} function valid(): bool {return $this->i<2;} function current(): mixed {return $this->i;} function key(): mixed {return $this->i;} function next(): void {$this->i++;} } foreach(new I as $v) echo $v;\\\\\\\")))))\\\\n  (testing \\\\\\\"IteratorAggregate supplies the live iterator\\\\\\\"\\\\n    (is (= \\\\\\\"23\\\\\\\" (:php/out (h/run-raw\\\\n                            \\\\\\\"<?php class I implements Iterator {private $i=2;function rewind():void{}function valid():bool{return $this->i<4;}function current(){return $this->i;}function key(){return $this->i;}function next():void{$this->i++;}} class A implements IteratorAggregate {function getIterator():Iterator{return new I;}} foreach(new A as $v)echo $v;\\\\\\\")))))\\\\n  (testing \\\\\\\"property iteration filters visibility from the calling scope\\\\\\\"\\\\n    (is (= \\\\\\\"aabc\\\\\\\" (:php/out (h/run-raw\\\\n                              \\\\\\\"<?php class P {public $a='a'; protected $b='b'; private $c='c'; function f(){foreach($this as $v)echo $v;}} $p=new P;foreach($p as $v)echo $v;$p->f();\\\\\\\")))))\\\\n  (testing \\\\\\\"ArrayAccess reads by value; Countable and Stringable dispatch\\\\\\\"\\\\n    (is (= \\\\\\\"43s\\\\\\\" (:php/out (h/run-raw\\\\n                             \\\\\\\"<?php class A implements ArrayAccess, Countable, Stringable {function offsetExists($x):bool{return true;} function offsetGet($x){return 4;} function offsetSet($x,$v):void{} function offsetUnset($x):void{} function count():int{return 3;} function __toString():string{return 's';}} $a=new A;echo $a[0],count($a),(string)$a;\\\\\\\"))))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(def ^:private opts\\\\n  {:make-stream tu/make-stream\\\\n   :capability-secret tu/secret\\\\n   :primitives vm/primitives\\\\n   :modules (h/host-registry)})\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(def ^:private load-semantic\\\\n  (vm/fresh-code-loader semantic/load-ast vm/ast-contract))\\\\n---\\\\ndescription: Build, lint, test commands, TDD guidelines, and bracket debugging for Clojure, ClojureScript, Node.js, and ClojureDart\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n# BUILD & TEST\\\\n\\\\n## Commands\\\\n\\\\n```sh\\\\n# Tests (Babashka runner)\\\\nbb test              # All three lanes (JVM, Node, Dart), fast default form: no slow tests\\\\nbb test:all          # Every test on every lane, slow ones included (JVM takes 20+ min)\\\\nbb test:slow         # Only the slow tests, on every lane\\\\n# One lane alone: <task>:clj, <task>:cljs, <task>:cljd\\\\nbb test:clj          # JVM, fast: skips ^:slow (bare `clj -M:test` runs them too)\\\\nbb test:cljs         # Node (shadow-cljs :cljs alias), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\\\\nbb test:cljd         # Dart (needs flutter on PATH), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\\\\nbb test:all:clj      # JVM, no filter: `clojure -M:test`\\\\nbb test:all:cljs     # Node with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\\\\nbb test:all:cljd     # Dart with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\\\\nbb test:slow:clj     # JVM: `-i :slow` (long-loops-test, ~14 min)\\\\nbb test:slow:cljs    # Node: only the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\\\\nbb test:slow:cljd    # Dart: only those namespaces' generated tests, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\\\\n# Slow tests: tag a deftest ^:slow. The JVM runner then excludes it from `bb test:clj`.\\\\n# Node and Dart have no tag filter, so a .cljc slow test also wraps its body in\\\\n# (dao.test-slow/guard \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\" (fn [] ...)); it prints SKIP unless DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1.\\\\n# Node and Dart select slow tests by NAMESPACE (derived by grepping `slow/guard`\\\\n# under test/), so the non-slow tests inside those namespaces also run there.\\\\n# On Node, shadow also runs the test namespaces those nine require (about\\\\n# seven more, e.g. lower-portable-test); on Dart only the nine namespaces run.\\\\n# Run test:slow / test:all before a big merge or a commit that touches many parts.\\\\n# Run one Dart lane at a time per machine (the limit is cores and the Flutter cache,\\\\n# not subsystems). On the many-core remote hosts see \\\\\\\"Remote test servers\\\\\\\" below for\\\\n# which lanes may overlap.\\\\n#\\\\n# When to tag a test slow: when it takes more than about 5 s on any lane (the\\\\n# Python e2e tests sit on a ~3 s floor, so their JVM cut is 3.0 s). The\\\\n# default lanes must stay in minutes; 22 JVM tests (0.75% of the suite) were\\\\n# 81% of its test time. Tag it ^:slow on the JVM; if it is a .cljc test, also\\\\n# wrap its body in dao.test-slow/guard so Node and Dart skip it by default. A\\\\n# test that is slow only on Dart (dao.jing.dht-test/unproven-chunks-... takes\\\\n# 72 s there, 3.6 s on the JVM) is a candidate for a speed investigation first.\\\\n# Python slow set (2026-10-06): 65 ^:slow and 15 guard-only tests in the\\\\n# yang.python.antlr e2e, e2e-c1, prelude-parity, safepoint, float-address\\\\n# and int-contract tests; a Python slice landing runs `bb test:sub:clj yang.python --slow`\\\\n# (or `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <ns>`).\\\\n# While iterating, use the Gate Ladder (see below): G0 iterate via `bb test:sub:clj <own>`\\\\n# or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`. Do not run the full `bb test` while iterating.\\\\n# When a test fails, reproduce and fix it by running ONLY the failing test\\\\n# (`clojure -M:test -n <ns> -v <ns>/<var>`, Node `--test=<ns>`, Dart `--only <ns>`) --\\\\n# never the whole suite (owner ruling 2026-11-01; see Gate Ladder G0).\\\\n# Individual tests run fine on the laptop; suite-scale runs (G1 subsystem sets,\\\\n# G2 changed sets, full suites, slow tier, nightly) run on shiva/jupiter --\\\\n# the suite has outgrown the laptop (owner ruling 2026-11-04).\\\\n# At slice checkpoints, run G1 (`bb test:sub <own>`). Before landing a slice, run\\\\n# G2 (`bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes).\\\\n# Full repo-wide `bb test` runs once daily on the remote hosts (04:00 VN);\\\\n# a MERGE needs only the affected tests (bb test:changed) -- owner ruling 2026-11-01;\\\\n# for a fix branch, the previously-failing tests green IS the merge bar\\\\n# (owner ruling 2026-11-07; see Gate Ladder G0).\\\\n# Cross-host bugs show only on Node or Dart, so tri-host verification is mandatory\\\\n# for every gate from G1 upward. Run one lane set at a time per machine to avoid\\\\n# contention (a laptop has 8 cores; the 24- and 48-core remote hosts have room to\\\\n# overlap lanes, see \\\\\\\"Remote test servers\\\\\\\" below).\\\\n# Measured fast-lane times (2026-10-03): bb test about 14 min = JVM 5.5 + Node\\\\n# 3.8 + Dart 4.3, plus builds. test:slow: Node and Dart about 5 min each (mostly\\\\n# compile); the JVM half is estimated at 17 min (long-loops-test alone is 14),\\\\n# not yet run end to end. test:all: JVM 20+ min, also an estimate.\\\\nnpm test             # Node.js tests\\\\n\\\\n# Cross-host peers the JVM lane spawns. `bb test` builds both. A bare\\\\n# `bb test:clj` builds only the Node REPL (it depends on build:yin-repl-node);\\\\n# without build:yin-repl-peer first, the Dart-peer tests skip with a printed notice.\\\\n# Under `bb test:sub` and `bb test:changed`, prerequisites are derived automatically.\\\\nbb build:yin-repl-peer   # Dart exe build/yin-repl-peer (yin.repl R5 pairs)\\\\nbb build:yin-repl-node   # Node REPL target/yin-repl.js; REQUIRED by\\\\n                         # yin.repl.dht-process-test (JVM-to-Node DHT reader,\\\\n                         # and the linker L5 Node reader that requires a module\\\\n                         # by name): `clojure -M:test` without it fails that test\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Changed-only tests: `bb test:changed`\\\\n\\\\n`bb test:changed` (src/dev/affected.clj) runs the fast tests a change can\\\\nreach: the reverse require closure of the files changed since the\\\\nmerge-base with master, plus fixtures that mention a changed resource path,\\\\ntests that walk a changed tree, and each src file's `_test` by convention.\\\\nA walker is a file calling file-seq, fs/glob, fs/list-dir,\\\\nfs/walk-file-tree or .listFiles; each string literal argument of its\\\\nio/file, fs/file, fs/path, fs/glob, java.io.File. or File. calls is a root\\\\n(let-bound roots count), and a change under a root selects it. The three\\\\nlanes run in parallel (logs: target/profile/changed-<lane>.log) after the\\\\nneeded builds. `test:changed:list` shows what and why; `:clj`/`:cljs`/\\\\n`:cljd` run one lane; `--base REF`; `--changed FILE...` (absolute OK; a\\\\ntypo, an empty list or the wrong cwd exits 1). Use it to iterate and to\\\\nland a slice confined to a package. Exit 2 (from :list too) is a wide\\\\nchange (deps.edn bb.edn shadow-cljs.edn mise.toml .cljstyle src/dev/\\\\nantlr/ .clj-kondo/ package*/pubspec*): it runs nothing; run `bb test`,\\\\nas for a change to the core everything requires (yin.vm engine,\\\\ndao.stream, codecs) and before a big merge. Not seen: dynamic loads\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ncollab/yang-php/1794566777000-engineer-p7b-ticks-b.gpt-6.1-terra.stdout.log:27:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_13\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"cat > test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p7b.cljc <<'EOF'\\\\n(ns yang.php.antlr.programs-p7b\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Hand-derived tick expectations pending the pinned PHP oracle pass.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(def prologue\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"function tick_handler() { echo 'T'; } register_tick_function('tick_handler'); \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(def fixtures\\\\n  [{:id :sequence, :source \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"declare(ticks=1) { echo 'A'; \\\\\\\"'$x = 1; echo '\\\\\\\"'B'; }\\\\\\\\\\\\\