l gates in this session:\\\\n\\\\n| Gate | Result | Duration |\\\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\\\n| `clojure -M:test -n yang.safepoint-test` | pass, 9 tests / 20 assertions | 3.802 s |\\\\n| `cljstyle check src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc` | pass | 0.2 s |\\\\n| `clojure -M:kondo --lint src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc` | 0 errors, 0 warnings | 6.5 s |\\\\n| PHP tick, lowering, prelude and e2e; Python trace gates | not run in this session | — |\\\\n\\\\nThe requested implementation and acceptance gates remain outstanding. Earlier green and timeout results are recorded in part B'\\\\\\\"'s findings; they are not new results from this session.\\\\nEOF\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ncollab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.stdout.log:45:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_23\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"git add src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc collab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md && git commit -m 'feat(php): declare statement ticks profile' && git push\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\ncollab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.stdout.log:46:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_23\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"git add src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc collab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md && git commit -m 'feat(php): declare statement ticks profile' && git push\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"Running formatters on staged files...\\\\nFormatting complete.\\\\n[p7b-ticks 38375bf7] feat(php): declare statement ticks profile\\\\n 2 files changed, 27 insertions(+)\\\\n create mode 100644 collab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md\\\\nTo github.com:sonwh98/datomworld.git\\\\n   411c2b08..38375bf7  p7b-ticks -> p7b-ticks\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ncollab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.stdout.log:47:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_24\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"**The PHP ticks integration is incomplete.** I added the independent `:after` ticks profile and pushed it in commit `38375bf7`, but it is not wired into execution. The staged fixtures remain red; the registry, statement-site lowering, firing rule, generator behavior, and linked include handoff are still outstanding.\\\\n\\\\nThe shared safepoint test passed (9 tests, 20 assertions), and the touched source file passed cljstyle and kondo. I did not run the PHP or Python gates in this session.\\\\n\\\\nThe task specifies a counter per `declare` site, while the cited slice-3 design describes a request-wide counter. The explicit task instruction takes precedence for implementation; I recorded the discrepancy for parity review.\\\\n\\\\nDetails and the predecessor’s include timeout command are in the [part C findings](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p7b/collab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md).\\\"}}\\n---\\ndescription: Lead System Architect role definition for datom.world\\n---\\n\\n# ROLE: Lead System Architect\\n\\n## Domain Scope\\n\\n- Foundational axioms, architectural invariants, and design contracts\\n- Subsystem boundaries, interpreters, host isolation, and explicit causality\\n- Cross-platform architecture, migration strategy, and compatibility boundaries\\n- ADR coherence, domain vocabulary, and theoretical grounding where useful\\n- Architecture review for high-risk or cross-cutting changes\\n- Commit sign-off: the sign-off on completed, review-reconciled work that\\n  authorizes the orchestrator to stage, commit, merge, and push it\\n  (trivial direct edits are exempt; see\\n  [`orchestrator.md`](orchestrator.md#coordination-contract))\\n\\nThis role owns no permanent file list. Each task defines the artifacts it may\\ninspect or change and any permitted expansion.\\n\\n## Core Responsibilities\\n\\n1. **Protect Invariants**: Strictly enforce the 6 non-negotiable invariants (no hidden global state, no implicit control flow, no raw callbacks, no shared mutable state, no layer collapsing, no assumed graphs).\\n2. **Decompose Complexity**: When new requirements emerge, decompose them into append-only streams, explicit interpreters, and immutable datom representations.\\n3. **Malleability Governance**: Ensure architecture adheres to bounded complexity, loose coupling, and high cohesion as defined in [`docs/agents/malleability.md`](../malleability.md).\\n4. **Lineage Alignment**: Keep designs grounded in Plan 9 / Datomic / Lisp architectural lineage.\\n\\n## Delegation Prompt Template\\n\\n```text\\nCreated-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\\nCreated-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\\n\\n# Task: <Task Name>\\n\\nRole: Lead System Architect\\n\\nImplementers:\\n- Model: <model-name> | Assigned: <local timestamp> | Status: active | Rationale: <why>\\n\\nPerform a read-only architecture review of <design-change>.\\n\\nRead first:\\n- docs/design/datom.world.md\\n- <target-design-file>\\n- <relevant-implementation-boundary>\\n- <relevant-contract-tests>\\n\\nEvaluate foundational invariants, ownership boundaries, explicit state and\\ncontrol flow, concurrency and linearization, dynamic extension, host isolation,\\nCLJ/CLJS/CLJD portability, migration risk, completion criteria, and design\\ncontradictions. Distinguish architectural defects from implementation gaps or\\nintentionally deferred work. Do not edit files.\\n\\nBegin the final response exactly with:\\nCompleted-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\\nCompleted-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\\n\\nThen report: severity | file:line | invariant/evidence | recommended correction.\\nAlso confirm the requested properties that passed review.\\n```\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/yang-php/1794567570000-architect-ticks-counter-ruling.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log:15:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"git status --short; git log -3 --oneline; cat collab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md; cat collab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.prompt.md; nl -ba test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p7b.cljc; rg -n 'ticks|P7-b' docs/design/yang.php.md; cat docs/agents/build-n-test.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"git: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-eFF2jOO4' (errno=Operation not permitted)\\n2026-11-13 18:00:09.901 xcodebuild[9263:128451675]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\\n2026-11-13 18:00:10.145 xcodebuild[9263:128451674] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \\\"Input/output error\\\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-yD8L12E5' (errno=Operation not permitted)\\n2026-11-13 18:00:11.135 xcodebuild[9269:128451723]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\\n2026-11-13 18:00:11.402 xcodebuild[9269:128451721] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \\\"Input/output error\\\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\\n?? collab/yang-php/1794566777000-engineer-p7b-ticks-b.gpt-6.1-terra.stdout.log\\n?? collab/yang-php/1794566777000-engineer-p