he design's table).\\n    21\\t- include site-set handoff: canonical published rows carry no marks; PHP receives the unit explicitly (design's landing requirement). The include red currently TIMES OUT — if your implementation doesn't fix the timeout in a reasonable budget, mark it in findings with the exact command + durations rather than leaving it hanging; the orchestrator reruns it remote if needed.\\n    22\\t\\n    23\\t## Gates (all sequential, generous timeouts)\\n    24\\t- ticks_test + yang.php tick/lowering/prelude focused namespaces green; yang.safepoint-test 9/20 stays green; python trace-basic + linked-tracing-profile green (additivity); affected e2e fast set; kondo 0/0 + cljstyle clean on touched files. Fixtures stay :oracle :pending — do NOT run docker.\\n    25\\t\\n    26\\t## Rules\\n    27\\t- Conventional commits on p7b-ticks; push as you go. No merges. Design gap -> stop that item + report.\\n    28\\t- Findings: collab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md (per-fixture red->green chronology, file:line, gate table with sequential timings, include-handoff status).\\n   479\\t(defn check-p7-fixture\\n   480\\t  \\\"Run a P7 fixture with its prologue and optional included units.\\\"\\n   481\\t  [dir {:keys [id source units out oracle]}]\\n   482\\t  (let [unit-dir (name id)\\n   483\\t        pre (str unit-dir \\\"/pre.php\\\")]\\n   484\\t    (doseq [[path contents] (merge units {\\\"main.php\\\" (str \\\"<?php \\\" source),\\n   485\\t                                          \\\"pre.php\\\" (p7-prologue)})]\\n   486\\t      (let [f (io/file dir unit-dir path)]\\n   487\\t        (io/make-parents f)\\n   488\\t        (write-source! dir (str unit-dir \\\"/\\\" path) contents)))\\n   489\\t    (let [actual (run-php-file-with-prepend dir \\\"main.php\\\" pre unit-dir)\\n   490\\t          expected {:out out, :diag [], :uncaught nil}]\\n   491\\t      {:id id, :oracle oracle,\\n   492\\t       :pass? (and (not= :pend